      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Nifedipine-induced gingival hypertrophy is a rare side effect reported by the producers of this drug but, surely, not well known in all its aspects. In the present case report this pathology is studied in a patient treated with nifedipine for 30 months for cardiac angina, analyzing the histologic features, the therapy plain conducted for the hypertrophy and the most important pathogenetic theories formulated till now."},
